IMPORT prelude

-- Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- superannuation: the spouse contribution tax offset (ss 290-230,
-- 290-235), the non-concessional contributions cap (ss 291-20(2), 292-85(2)), downsizer contributions (s 292-102), the transfer
-- balance cap (ss 294-30, 294-35), member benefits at 60 (ss 301-10, 301-15) and death benefits (ss 302-60, 302-140, 302-145,
-- 302-195).
--
-- SEAT: the taxpayer -- an individual Australian resident who contributes to super, draws a pension from it, or receives a
-- death benefit from someone else's ("Is my pension taxed?", "Is the super I receive taxed?").
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 267, compilation date 27 August 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 79, 2026; register id
-- C2026C00400, 12 volumes), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A05138.txt. The contributions caps and the
-- transfer balance cap for any year after 2017-18 are indexed amounts (Subdiv 960-M) that the Act does not print; they are
-- passed in.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Indexation itself (s 960-285); the bring-forward of the non-concessional cap (s 292-85(3)-(8)); the age and work
-- tests in the SIS Regulations; transfer balance credits and debits in detail (Subdivs 294-B, 294-C) and proportional indexation
-- (s 294-40); elements untaxed in the fund (Subdiv 301-C, ss 302-85, 302-90); the low rate cap (s 301-20); income streams to
-- dependants under 60 (ss 302-70, 302-75); defined benefit income (Div 303); the tax free and taxable components themselves
-- (Subdiv 307-C); interdependency (s 302-200) beyond one fact.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No
-- pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 -- superannuation`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `290-230, 290-235 -- spouse contribution tax offset`

-- s 290-230(2): only if the person was your spouse, both were Australian residents when you contributed, and "(c) the total of
-- your spouse's: (i) assessable income ...; and (ii) *reportable fringe benefits total; and (iii) *reportable employer
-- superannuation contributions; for the income year is less than $40,000"; (3) not if "living separately and apart ... on a
-- permanent basis"; (4A) not if the spouse exceeded the non-concessional cap or had a total superannuation balance at or above
-- the general transfer balance cap (one fact).
-- s 290-235(1): the offsets "cannot exceed 18% of the lesser of the following: (a) $3,000 reduced by the amount (if any) by
-- which the total mentioned in paragraph 290-230(2)(c) for the income year exceeds $37,000; (b) the sum of the *spouse
-- contributions you make in the income year." (2) "The maximum *tax offset ... is $540".
@export What tax offset do I get for contributing to my spouse's super (ss 290-230, 290-235)?
GIVEN `spouse income total` IS A NUMBER @desc Your spouse's assessable income, reportable fringe benefits and reportable employer super contributions for the year, in dollars
      `spouse contributions` IS A NUMBER @desc What you contributed to your spouse's super in the year, in dollars
      `both resident and living together` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were both Australian residents and not living separately and apart permanently
      `spouse over a cap` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse exceeded the non-concessional cap or had a total super balance at or above the general transfer balance cap
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What spouse contribution offset do I get` MEANS
    IF `both resident and living together` AND (NOT `spouse over a cap`) AND `spouse income total` LESS THAN 40000
    THEN `the lesser of` 540 (`the lesser of` (3000 MINUS (`the greater of` (`spouse income total` MINUS 37000) 0)) `spouse contributions` TIMES 18 DIVIDED BY 100)
    ELSE 0

§§ `291-20(2), 292-85(2) -- non-concessional contributions cap`

-- s 291-20(2): the concessional contributions cap is "(a) for the 2017-2018 financial year -- $25,000; or (b) for the 2018-2019
-- financial year or a later financial year -- the amount worked out by indexing annually" (passed in).
-- s 292-85(2): the non-concessional contributions cap is "(a) ... 4 times your *concessional contributions cap under subsection
-- 291-20(2) for the year; or (b) if, immediately before the start of the year, your *total superannuation balance equals or
-- exceeds the *general transfer balance cap for the year -- nil."
@export What is my non-concessional contributions cap for the year (s 292-85(2))?
GIVEN `concessional contributions cap` IS A NUMBER @desc The concessional contributions cap for the year (indexed; $25,000 for 2017-18)
      `total superannuation balance` IS A NUMBER @desc Your total super balance just before the start of the year, in dollars
      `general transfer balance cap` IS A NUMBER @desc The general transfer balance cap for the year, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my non-concessional cap` MEANS
    IF `total superannuation balance` AT LEAST `general transfer balance cap` THEN 0
    ELSE 4 TIMES `concessional contributions cap`

§§ `292-102 -- downsizer contributions`

-- s 292-102(1): covered if "(a) ... made ... in respect of you when you are aged 55 years or over"; (b) from the capital proceeds
-- of disposing of an ownership interest in a dwelling; (c) you or your spouse held it; (d) the gain or loss is "wholly or
-- partially disregarded under Subdivision 118-B"; (e) the 10-year condition in (2); (f) "located in *Australia, and is not a
-- caravan, houseboat or other mobile home"; (g) "made within 90 days, or such longer period as the Commissioner allows, after the
-- time the change of ownership occurs"; (h) you choose; (i) no earlier downsizer contribution from another dwelling.
-- (3): only to the extent it does not exceed the lesser of "(a) $300,000, less any other contribution that is already covered
-- ... in respect of you; and (b) the sum of the *capital proceeds" from the interest and any related spousal interest, less
-- other downsizer contributions from them.
DECLARE Downsizer HAS
    `age when contributing` IS A NUMBER
    `main residence exemption applied at least partly` IS A BOOLEAN
    `years held by the couple before the disposal` IS A NUMBER
    `dwelling in Australia and not mobile` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days after the change of ownership` IS A NUMBER
    `Commissioner allowed longer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `chosen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `earlier downsizer from another dwelling` IS A BOOLEAN
    `amount contributed` IS A NUMBER
    `your earlier downsizer contributions` IS A NUMBER
    `capital proceeds of both interests` IS A NUMBER
    `other downsizer contributions from these proceeds` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the contribution` IS A Downsizer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contribution qualifies as a downsizer contribution` IF
        `the contribution`'s `age when contributing` AT LEAST 55
    AND `the contribution`'s `main residence exemption applied at least partly`
    AND `the contribution`'s `years held by the couple before the disposal` AT LEAST 10
    AND `the contribution`'s `dwelling in Australia and not mobile`
    AND (`the contribution`'s `days after the change of ownership` AT MOST 90 OR `the contribution`'s `Commissioner allowed longer`)
    AND `the contribution`'s `chosen`
    AND (NOT `the contribution`'s `earlier downsizer from another dwelling`)

@export How much of my contribution counts as a downsizer contribution (s 292-102)?
GIVEN `the contribution` IS A Downsizer @desc The contribution you made from the sale of your home
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is my downsizer contribution` MEANS
    IF `the contribution qualifies as a downsizer contribution` `the contribution`
    THEN `the lesser of` (`the contribution`'s `amount contributed`)
                         (`the lesser of` (300000 MINUS `the contribution`'s `your earlier downsizer contributions`)
                                          (`the contribution`'s `capital proceeds of both interests` MINUS `the contribution`'s `other downsizer contributions from these proceeds`))
    ELSE 0

§§ `294-30, 294-35 -- transfer balance cap`

-- s 294-35(3): "The general transfer balance cap is: (a) for the 2017-2018 *financial year -- $1,600,000; or (b) for the
-- 2018-2019 financial year or a later financial year -- the amount worked out by indexing annually" (passed in).
-- (1): your cap for the year you first have a transfer balance account equals the general cap for that year.
-- s 294-30(1): "You have excess transfer balance at a particular time if, at that time, the *transfer balance in your *transfer
-- balance account exceeds your *transfer balance cap".
@export What is my transfer balance cap in the year I first start a retirement pension (s 294-35)?
GIVEN `first financial year starting` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which that financial year begins
      `indexed general cap for that year` IS A NUMBER @desc The indexed general transfer balance cap for that year (after 2017-18)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my transfer balance cap` MEANS
    IF `first financial year starting` EQUALS 2017 THEN 1600000 ELSE `indexed general cap for that year`

@export Do I have an excess transfer balance, and how much (s 294-30)?
GIVEN `credits` IS A NUMBER @desc Transfer balance credits (for example the value of pensions started), in dollars
      `debits` IS A NUMBER @desc Transfer balance debits (for example commutations), in dollars
      `transfer balance cap` IS A NUMBER @desc Your transfer balance cap, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my excess transfer balance` MEANS
    `the greater of` (`credits` MINUS `debits` MINUS `transfer balance cap`) 0

§§ `301-10, 301-15 -- member benefits`

-- s 301-10: "If you are 60 years or over when you receive a *superannuation benefit, the benefit is not assessable income and is
-- not *exempt income." (Note 2: an element untaxed in the fund -- Subdiv 301-C, not encoded.)
-- Under 60 the taxable component is assessable (ss 301-20 to 301-40), with offsets not encoded; the tax free component is not
-- assessable at any age (ss 301-15, 301-30).
@export How much of my super benefit from a taxed fund is assessable income (ss 301-10 to 301-40)?
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age when you receive the benefit
      `taxable component` IS A NUMBER @desc The taxable component of the benefit, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of my super benefit is assessable` MEANS
    IF `age` AT LEAST 60 THEN 0
    ELSE `taxable component`

§§ `302-60, 302-140, 302-145, 302-195 -- death benefits`

-- s 302-195(1): "A death benefits dependant, of a person who has died, is: (a) the deceased person's *spouse or former spouse; or
-- (b) the deceased person's *child, aged less than 18; or (c) any other person with whom the deceased person had an
-- interdependency relationship under section 302-200 just before he or she died; or (d) any other person who was a dependant of
-- the deceased person just before he or she died."
-- s 302-60: "A *superannuation lump sum that you receive because of the death of a person of whom you are a *death benefits
-- dependant is not assessable income and is not *exempt income."
-- s 302-140: for a non-dependant, the tax free component "is not assessable income"; s 302-145(1) "the *taxable component of
-- the lump sum is assessable income"; (2) an offset ensures "the rate of income tax on the *element taxed in the fund of the lump
-- sum does not exceed 15%"; (3) on the element untaxed in the fund, 30%.
DECLARE Recipient IS ONE OF
    `the spouse or former spouse`
    `a child under 18`
    `an adult child`
    `someone else`

@export Am I a death benefits dependant of the person who died (s 302-195)?
GIVEN `recipient` IS A Recipient @desc How you were related to the person who died
      `interdependent or dependent just before the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had an interdependency relationship with, or were a dependant of, the person just before the death
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a death benefits dependant` IF
    CONSIDER `recipient`
    WHEN `the spouse or former spouse` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a child under 18` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE `interdependent or dependent just before the death`

@export How much of a super death benefit lump sum paid to me is assessable income (ss 302-60, 302-140, 302-145)?
GIVEN `recipient` IS A Recipient @desc How you were related to the person who died
      `interdependent or dependent just before the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had an interdependency relationship with, or were a dependant of, the person just before the death
      `taxable component` IS A NUMBER @desc The taxable component of the lump sum, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of the death benefit is assessable to me` MEANS
    IF `Am I a death benefits dependant` `recipient` `interdependent or dependent just before the death`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `taxable component`

@export What is the most I can be taxed on the taxable component of a death benefit, in percent (s 302-145(2), (3))?
GIVEN `element untaxed in the fund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the amount is an element untaxed in the fund
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most I can be taxed on the death benefit in percent` MEANS
    IF `element untaxed in the fund` THEN 30 ELSE 15
